  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="FR">5- Local partners and targeted groups build capacity in wash business development, technical knowledge, life skills and partnerships for local businesses.</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="FR">Enterprise is able to systematically collect, monitor, analyse and report on impact (data).</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="FR">Enterprise has developed an internal IMM system, i.e. i) impact strategy/Theory of Change, ii) data collection strategy/process/templates, iii) data collection and monitoring system, iv) impact/decision-making report template. Hence, the enterprise is fully prepared for the next phase (beyond the scope of this TA project), i.e. to operationalise the IMM system by developing surveys, collecting baseline (impact) data, periodically update these data, create impact reports and use them to steer operational decision-making.</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2022">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="FR">Enterprise has no formal impact focus at all; no KPIs, nor impact indicators. The enterprise has to build an IMM strategy and system from scratch. The TA support will focus on raising awareness on the value of IMM (insight in and demonstration of impact) and getting the enterprises acquainted with concepts, tools and frameworks.</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <baseline year="2022"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-12-31"></period-end>
     <actual value="All deliverables related to setting up an Impact Measurement and Management (IMM) system/process have been successfully completed, i.e.: 1) Description of problem, solutions, revenue model; 2) Impact Model and Impact Statement; 3) Customer Promise Sheet; 4) Comprehensive Theory of Change; 5) Customer Touchpoint Journey; 6) Data Collection Plan; 7) Data Analysis and Review System; 8) Decision-Making Report. The next phase (beyond the scope of this TA project) is to operationalise the IMM system, e.g. development of surveys, collection of actual data and data analysis."></actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-12-31"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="FR">Enterprise is fully prepared to start raising (repayable) funding</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="FR">Enterprise has all documents in place that are required for fundraising (e.g. pitch decks, terms sheet) and a data room available for when funders request information. Hence, the enterprise is fully prepared for the next phase (beyond the scope of this TA project), i.e. to raise (repayable) investment, demonstrated by a signed terms sheet, Expression of Interest (EoI) or actual funding/investment agreement.</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2022">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="FR">FlexEAU is looking for various funding sources (of long-term financing) in order to bridge the public funding gap and to compensate for losses due to suspended investment in assets by the government. They are in conversations with various (impact) investors, hence any support will be useful. The enterprise is mainly looking for expansion of solarized boreholes (20 additional). Enterprise has several funding leads, but there is a big gap between realised vs. targeted fundraising. Relevant documents for fundraising (e.g. pitchdeck) are outdated and there is no clear and realistic fundraising strategy.</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <baseline year="2022"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-12-31"></period-end>
     <actual value="All deliverables related to Investment Readiness (IR) have been successfully completed, i.e.: 1) Pitch Deck; 2) Investor Valuation Memorandum; 3) Financial Model; 4) Financial Instrument Advisory; 5) Investor hitlist and Introductions; 6) Priced Round Term Sheet; 7) Investor Data Room; 8) Periodic Business Report; 9) Growth Metrics; 10) Recommendation Report. The next phase (beyond the scope of this TA project) is to raise (repayable) investment, demonstrated by a signed terms sheet, Expression of Interest (EoI) or actual funding/investment agreement."></actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-12-31"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
